MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Twelfth Challenge/Solution pair. Proves the Beta integral
∫₀^R x^u (R−x)^v = R^{u+v+1} u! v!/(u+v+1)! and, by Fubini and induction on the
dimension, ∫_{z≥0, Σz≤R} ∏ zᵢ^{eᵢ} = R^{m+Σe} ∏ eᵢ!/(m+Σe)!, with the m = 0, R = 0,
R < 0 and volume cases. At rational R the integral equals V0's simplexMoment,
and rational polynomials integrate to an explicit rational (Lemma 10.1 on the
simplex). Comparator suite simplex_moment_v1 added (12 suites); controls and
result record included. Axioms: propext, Quot.sound, Classical.choice.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
